  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policies and strategies adopted and actional programmes implemented for inclusive skills training and lifelong learning providing equal opportunities for vulnerable groups</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">China is advancing a more responsive, inclusive, and sustainable labour market through lifelong skills development, but faces challenges including skills mismatches, insufficient implementation measures of vocational training, and barriers to inclusive employment for persons with disabilities and people living with HIV. Building on momentum from government-led initiatives including Skills for a Brighter Future and growing commitments to more inclusive employment, the ILO is cooperating with Chinese stakeholders to strengthen lifelong learning, quality apprenticeships, and social inclusion, especially for vulnerable groups. The ILO will support policymakers and practitioners through policy advice, skills toolkits, institutional capacity building, and targeted training. Expected results include: Government adopted and strengthened skills and lifelong learning strategies to enhance workers&#x2019; employability in the digital and green transition; Government and key national stakeholders developed and strengthened innovative and inclusive work-based learning programmes responsive to technological transformation and green transition; Government and key national stakeholders developed and strengthened strategies and action plans to enhance youth employment;  Persons with disabilities gain clearer pathways and targeted digital skills training aligned with local labour-market needs, leading to improved job-readiness and increased access to digital employment opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
